CORE libstdcxx
main.cpp
--cpp11 --object-bits 12 --unwind 12 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ no read error: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ failed: 0, a limit, or nothing extracted: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Fixed: the num_get facet was not modelled (a nondeterministic facet
pointer; __check_facet called std::__throw_bad_cast, which has no
body), so cin.fail() always held.  The "C" locale's num_get facet is
now provided like num_put (classic_num_put), and libstdc++'s own
do_get parses the unknown input.
